# Thrustmaster T16000M (stick alone) as the RHC of the shuttle. Copy to "Joystick<N>.cfg" or "<device name>.cfg" (see DetectedDevices.txt).
# Axis names are the usual ones for this stick: check them with Ctrl+J in the simulation and change the SUBDEVID column if needed.
# Stick forward = pitch down, stick back = pitch up (like an aircraft), stick right = roll right, twist clockwise = yaw right.
# If a direction is wrong, change true to false (or false to true) in the REVERSE column of that line.
INPUT	SUBDEVID	REVERSE	DEADZONE	EXPO	CENTER
RHC_PITCH	Axis Y	false	0.03	0.3	0
RHC_ROLL	Axis X	false	0.03	0.3	0
RHC_YAW	Axis RZ	false	0.05	0.4	0
RMS_CAPTURE	Button 0	false
RMS_RELEASE	Button 1	false
RMS_RATE_HOLD	Button 2	false
RMS_RATE_TOGGLE	Button 3	false
RMS_CONTROL_TOGGLE	Button 4	false
